The recursive version handles one node at a time. First, the rest of the list is cleaned. Then the current node is compared with the next node. If they have the same value, the current node is kept and the next duplicate is removed.

A dry run for `1 <-> 1 <-> 2` returns to the first `1`, skips the second `1`, and connects the first node to `2`.

